>   can send me some mail, I would appreciate it.  Please don't post 
>   a follow-up to this group.  Thanks.

I'm assuming you are talking about OpenVMS...

I think that you will find that most multi-user machines don't have
have problems with viruses. Believe it or not but I haven't heard of
any viruses that infect OpenVMS VAX or AXP. This is probably because
the vast majority of users on multi-user systems are prevented from
modifying kernel code and files. A user can corrupt their own files,
but can't corrupt the Operating System files.

Having said that, you should probably read guide to OpenVMS security.
Sorry I don't remember the exact name. There is also a product DEC
sells called DECinspect that reports on and helps inforce customizable
security rules.

Hope this helps...

