 From the MicroVAX Maintenance Information:

Table 7-1 provides a description of each test executed....test numbers
displayed on the MivroVAX II CPU I/O distribution insert while each test is
being run.  The number is also displayed in binary form by a series of red LEDs
on teh KA630-a module...

LED     Test
F       WAIT FOR DCOK
D       WAITING FOR POK
D       RUNNING CHECKSUM TEST ON CPU ROM
C       SEARCHING FOR RAM MEMORY REQUIRED FOR CPU ROM PROGRAMS
B       READ KA630-A IPCR REGISTER (accesses Q22-Bus)
A       TESTING VCB01 VIDEO CONSOLE DISPLAY (if present)
9       IDENTIFYING CONSOLE TERMINAL
8       LANGUAGE INQUIRY OR CPU HALTED
7       RUNNING DATA TESTS ON RAM MEMORY
6       RUNNING ADDRESS TESTS ON RAM MEMORY
5        RUNNING TESTS TAT USE Q22-BUS MAP TO ACCESS LOCAL MEMORY
4       CPU INSTRUCTION AND REGISTER TESTS
3       RUNNING INTERRUPT TESTS
2       SEARCHING FOR BOOTSTRAP DEVICE
1       BOOTSTRAP DEVICE FOUND
0       TESTING COMPLETED

