No, it's probably just a malfunctioning or mistuned network.

Assuming that by "VMS-machine" you mean VAX, I replicated your
experiment (DECnet COPY between two machines in different areas), 
and here's what I found:

AXP 3000/400 -> VAXstation 4090  2700 blocks/20.60 sec = .537 Mbps
VAXstation 4090 -> VS 4090	 2700 blocks/22.26 sec = .497 Mbps

So, no, looks like everything worked fine.

Now, all my systems had PIPELINE QUOTA set to 4032.  With higher
values, sometimes a more powerful sender can overrun a wimpy
receiver, resulting in heavy drops and retransmits.  Is this what
you encountered?

