In article <31460n$dhh@search01.news.aol.com>, terru@aol.com (Terru)
writes:

>Anyone know how to connect a 10baseT hub that has an AUI port, routing
>Novell IPX to a DEC DELNI routing LAT???
>I've tried simply running a transceiver cable from the AUI port on the
>10baseT hub to the DELNI port 2, but I get collisions on the 10baseT hub.

>Any ideas???

Could the collisions you see on the 10BaseT hub be normal for your
network?  
The method you described for connecting the hub to the DELNI should
probably have worked.  The DELNI is nothing more than a multiport repeater
(not a router).  Typically you tap the DELNI on to the thickwire using a
tranciver such as an H4005. This then gives you a bunch of ports that
behave pretty much like H4005s on the thickwire. (Provided a few of
ethernet specs like cable length and number of repeating segements don't
hang you.)  
You might check the 10BaseT hub for some of the following:
1. Is the AUI port Enabled?
2. Is bridging (if any) enabled for that segement?
3. Is the AUI cable good?

-Mark Clancy
MGClancy@aol.com

One last point: LAT is not routable! (A point frequently made to my
managers!!!)





