> |>Perhaps you just forgot to put the terminal server into some 8-bit-clean
> |>mode?  I am using the following sequence with a DECserver 200:
[...]

> |>    set port loss dis
> I can't set this (no privilege).  Does it matter?

It prevents the terminal server from emitting ^G (beep) whenever characters
are lost.  Perhaps you don't need this once you have reliable flow
control.  However, it should be possible to set this mode without
special privileges; then again, I don't know the DECserver 700.
You could also "define" this as the default (using the priv password).

> I should have noted that the port is set for XON/XOFF flow-control when first 
> connecting.  With DECUS UUCP (VMS), uucico changes this to RTS/CTS.  I had
> assumed that Taylor UUCP's uucico does this, but maybe this is the problem.

How should Taylor UUCP know that you want the remote modem to talk RTS/CTS
to the terminal server?

Add this to your startup script:

    set port flow cts

You definitely should make this the default in your terminal server.

