>Does anyone know how a Southern Hemisphere variant of a monitor varies
>from a Northern Hemisphere model ?

I beleive it is to do with the difference in alignment of the earth's magnetic 
field between the northern and southern hemispheres and how it affects the 
image displayed on the monitor.

When DEC first started shipping either  the VT200 or VT300 series terminals 
(can't recall which one) to NZ, they discovered that the raster scan 
pattern was distorted and each terminal had to be individually 
realigned by repositioning little alignment magnets on the CRT. Kept a few FS 
engineers busy for a while.

Didn't seem to worry the VT100's though.

Dave


