I didn't see the original note, but if this 3000 is an Alpha AXP system,
you just need to do the following:

boot -fl s

This takes you into single user mode.

boot -fl 2

which takes you to multi user mode, but without xdm started up.

If you manage to log in somehow with windows up, you can stop it like this:

/sbin/init.d/xdm stop

and start it like this:

/sbin/init.d/xdm start

These are about the only System V features I like!
