The following is valid for the 2000/300.  I think it holds for the
bigger boys too.

Press the halt button to get the console prompt (>>>).

>>>set boot_osflags s
>>>b

This will boot you in single-user mode, which won't be DECWindows
unless you've done really strange things to the init files.

You'll might need to do a
mount -w /
to make the root filesystem read-write.

Use ed to fix the passwd file.

Shutdown -h, change the boot_osflags back to "a", and boot again.
Everything should be fine.

(Is anyone maintaining an FAQ for this group?  This seems a natural
for it.)

