This sounds like your are using AF which was produced by one of our
research groups.  It isn't an officially supported product, but there's
a mailing list which can probably help answer your questions.  You can
subscribe by sending mail to af-request@crl.dec.com.

AF also supports mixing of audio streams, so, again, closing and reopening
the audio device is unnecessary, but should work.

The latest version of Multimedia Services for OSF/1 is V1.2 and the
lastest release of AF is AF3R1.  If you have earlier versions installed,
it would be worth upgrading to see if that fixes your problems.
 
