Actually, the DECchip 21064A *IS* EV4.5, a.k.a. EVshrink.  It's a .5 micron
implementation of the DECchip 21064 EV4 architecture with expanded caches
and improved branch prediction.  Even though the 21064A is produced via
the CMOS5 process, it is not EV5.

EV5, due out this Fall, will feature architctural improvements, quad-issue
superscalar support and a pretty substantial performance boost.  Word from
reliable sources has it that a quad-processor EV5-based TurboLaser will
do better than 1GFLOP.  Not too shabby.

For more details on EV5, check out the HOT Chips VI Symposium at Stanford
University, August 14-16 '94.










