I don't recall seeing any DEC BASIC developers posting to this
group.  If you post or mail me a self-contained example, I'll
pass it along.

Although DEC BASIC is a "V1", it started with the front end code
for VAX BASIC and shares the backend technology with most of
our other Alpha compilers.  Those 2 parts of the technology are
quite mature.

The VAX BASIC compiler didn't optimize, or at least not very
much.  We have seen occasions where application bugs only appear
with optimization turned on.  We've also seen occasions where
optimizers have bugs.  We can't tell about this case until we
see a test program.  
