Pardon my rewrapping your post, so it fits in 80 columns.

INTERNAL DRIVES
---------------

The DEC 3000 can have up to four 3.5" half-heighth SCSI-2 disks,
not counting the required cd-rom drive.

EXTERNAL DRIVES
---------------

The DEC 3000/500 has two SCSI adaptor, SCSI-A (internal) and SCSI-B
external. Almost any SCSI-2 disk will work, if it passes the tests
the VMS scsi disk driver makes (some Quantum drives don't).

Seagate ST12400N drives will work, since they're sold as RZ28Bs by DEC.
We have had ST11200Ns on our ALPHA running OpenVMS AXP V1.5 with no
problems. Seagate has a BBS where you can get the specs for all of
their drives: 408/438-8771 (8bits,no parity, one stop bit).

We purchased a DEC StorageWorks enclosure (BA350-KA, I think) for our
ALPHA, which supports hot disk swaps and additions. The cost is
~$950, plus cable. The StorageWorks trays can be purchased separately
if you want to add 3rd-party disks.


