In article <2uv44t$505@ghost.shsu.edu>, horn@oliver.shsu.edu (James T. Horn) writes:
>
>With the removing of Wpsplus from Allin1/AXP, is Digital looking at having
>something that will convert all a persons Wpsplus documents to WordPerfect
>from within All-in-1/AXP? Any information will be greatly appreciated.
>                      
For most sites, it would not be necesary to convert ALL existing WPSPLUS
documents from WPSPLUS to WPCORP.

Since the WPCORP editor is integrated at the DSAB level, the user can simply 
set the DEFAULT Editor to WPCORP, and from then on, the user DOES NOT NEED to
be concerned with whether a document is in WPSPLUS format, or WPCORP, or
whatever.

Simply editing the document from the ALL-IN-1 menu, will convert the
document - IF NEEDED to WPCORP from whatever format it was originally in.  For
most user transitions from WPSPLUS to WPCORP, most users need not worry about 
it. It is transparent to the user (i.e. the user doesn't have to do anything 
special to accomodate different formatted documents).

Note: When editing a document from the ALL-IN-1 menu with a editor other than
that of the document (i.e. a .WPL file being edited w/ WPCORP), ALL-IN-1
converts the file to the DEFAULT Editor format.  Upon exiting the editor, the
document is converted BACK to it's original format.

The most likely reason that a person, or company would need to do MASS
conversion of documents would be if there are documents that are constantly being
edited, update, and changed.  In this case, since there are some advanced
WPCORP features that are not supported in WPSPLUS (i.e. graphics, fonts,
tables, spreadsheet links, etc.), you would not want to be constantly going
through a DSAB conversion, back and forth from WPSPLUS to WPCORP.  In
this case, YES - A MASS CONVERSION of these types of documents would be
preferable.

For this need, there is currently no "conversion routine" developed by either
WPCORP or DIGITAL.  Though it would be a relatively simple matter to develope
a ALL-IN-1 script to go through each record in a FILE CABINET (DOCDB.DAT file)
and using ALL-IN-1 routines, convert the documents to WPCORP via. the DSAB.
WordPerfect Corp. OpenVMS Customer Services will be working on a "suggested
method, a very basic example" to accomplish this.  Since this type of routine
would need to be developed for each site's needs, only a very basic concept of
routines needed can be given.

I hope this helps.

Kevin Hehl
