Hmmm...these come in 8-port and 16-port flavors.  I have both types
here.  I think the 16-port doesn't have all the modem control you'd
need for SLIP/PPP.  I've used a pair of 8-port models talking SLIP
to eachother which worked, though they work much better if you have
them talking to something OTHER than another instance of itself.
Go figger...

There is also a cabling issue.  The 8-port model has RS-232 ports
on the back (standard size), while the 16-port model uses rj-45
modular plugs (much more convenient to build cables).

: I am soliciting information about the DecServer on a Sun system.
: Thanks for any help that you can give.

Can't help you there.  Mine all talk to a BSDI/386 box.  They're
great terminal servers.  You can probably find the 8 port models
for 7-900 bucks and the 16-port models for 1000-1200 bucks.  You'll
also want to upgrade the RAM to 5mb and make sure you can get the
software for them for your Sun (they don't boot off flash RAM and
need a host with the software to kickstart).

Chris
