>five 16MByte machines that I want to upgrade to 32MByte, but someone told me 
>that they can only go up to 24MByte. Any comments on upgrade costs would
>also be welcome

Yes, that's right.  The DS3100 (and DS2100) can only go to 24MB.  We have
hundreds of them (unfortunately).  Their memory limitations are really
their worst handicap.  I suppose if some third party vendor really wanted
to, they could find a way around that limit, but I haven't heard of any
doing it, and I suspect it's a little late for anyone to start now.

In any event, they're not bad little machines.  You can do a lot with them
as long as you stay away from those memory-hungry X11 applications.

