Transitioning Financial Support Option??? Sounds like a New Age replacement
for Digital's previous layoff-related phrase: involuntary redeployment!

With respect to the imminent sale of a portion of Digital's storage
business, this is but the tip of the iceberg.  We believe that Digital
will within the couple of weeks unveil a major restructuring initiative
which will be replete with workforce reductions (~20K is not out of the
realm of possibility), additional unit divestitures (portions of 
semiconductor operations, networking and service/support are said to be 
on the block) and a drastic downsizing of the firm's layered software
portfolio.

One bright spot in the storage business divestiture: Digital is holding onto
its video server and StorageWorks operations.  Video servers represent 
what is arguably Alpha AXP's last best chance to flourish beyond DEC's
traditional installed base, and StorageWorks has good brand name
recognition and a loyal following.  Accordingly, Digital can't be accused 
of taking a Pan Am approach to downsizing, e.g. selling off all the 
family jewels and retaining holdings that are of dubious value.



