We've had both HP's (III Si in our case) and LPS 1700.  The only problem we've
had with the LPS was some HP users who we're using HP specific compressed print
(narrow font) capabilities.

I showed them they could simulate this through DCPS+'s PCL converter.  The
command to request compressed print causes the HP's printer software to insert
a PCL command.

The problem we had with the HP was using HP's ethernet card.  It only supports
one connection at a time, even connecting from two HP's failed.  If you go with
HP, go with one of the third part cards.

