sysdhw@atscv1.atsc.allied.com wrote:

>I have come into possession of a DEC LAN Bridge 150 ethernet bridge.
>I haven't found the docs for it, and I'd like to know what the set of
>6 dip switches and jumper on the back of the unit are for.  Can anyone
>dig into their docs and have a look?

>Any help is appreciated,
>Dave

Hi.

dip switches    1 2 3 4 5 6

1 : loop self-test
2 : nvram reset
3 : port A access
4 : port B access
5 : down-line load enabled
6 : not used

If you are installing the LAN Bridge 150 unit as a LTM Listener, set switch 5,
down-line load enabled, to ON (down=ON).

LTM=LAN Traffic Minitor.

If you are installing the LAN Bridge to operate as a bridge, whenever power is
applied to the unit, the bridge performs its diagnostic self-test (about 15
seconds), then spends about 30 seconds communicating with other bridges in the
network to determine if there are loops and at the same time builds its initial 
database of forwarding addresses.

If the DC OK LED, Test LED, and Port A and B LEDs are lit, the unit is
operating properly and the logical link can be check.

I hope this help you.



--
